      "assessment": "The root cause is bad release 1.5 on payments (confidence 0.85), which also wrote 166 duplicate payments to the ledger. The incident commander itself rolled payments back from 1.5 to 1.3, and the rollback completed; the latest of two recovery looks was clean.",
      "recommendation": "The ledger issue has been escalated (soon) to the on-call engineer: a person must reconcile and resolve the 166 duplicate payments through the bank's correction process, without reversing, refunding or editing postings outside that process. Operations should review the money and ledger effects of these duplicates, and keep payments on 1.3 until release 1.5 is fixed."
    },
